  "answer": "This looks like the same problem as PowerToys#46587. \"Open url in Edge\" is a fallback command, and pinning a fallback to the Dock registers the pin but never shows it on the Dock. A maintainer said in that ticket that fallbacks generally shouldn't be pinnable, because they exist to turn a typed query into an action. No fix for pinning fallbacks was announced there. As a workaround, pin a regular item instead of the fallback. The same ticket says pinning a shortcut works, and PowerToys#49025 shows bookmarks can be pinned too. So save the msteams:// link as a bookmark or shortcut and pin that. Please also follow PowerToys#46587 for updates."
 },
